    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1305">

                <pb facs="1030" n="954" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg954"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.77/232</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister of Panama </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Legation’s note No. 235
                    of February 28, 1916, I have the honor to transmit herewith a copy of a letter
                    from Judge Frank Feuille, Special Attorney for the Panama Canal, to General
                    George W. Goethals, U. S. A., Governor of the Panama Canal, relative to the
                    legal status of the Panama Railroad Company.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d1305-f1"/>
                    Governor Goethals concurs in the conclusions of Judge Feuille that, in view of
                    the concessions to the Panama Railroad Company and of the provisions of the
                    Treaty of 1903, the claims advanced are without foundation and there is nothing
                    open to arbitration.</p>
                <p>The Department is of the opinion that the authorities of the Panama Canal have
                    made a complete and satisfactory statement in answer to the contentions advanced
                    in the note of Minister Morales.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
